From 8b4a0c7f21106fe5e9a57b6a3afb66e6a8bc078a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cynthia Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:33:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep `n_neighbors - 1` neighbors in `distances` for all
 kNN transformers

Since the transformer refactor (#2536), `Neighbors.compute_neighbors` only
restricted `.distances` to the `n_neighbors - 1` nearest neighbors on the
brute-force shortcut path. For every other transformer the raw
`fit_transform` output was stored, and `PyNNDescentTransformer` (used
explicitly or by default for >= 8192 cells) returns `n_neighbors` neighbors
plus the cell itself, so `.obsp["distances"]` had one neighbor more per row
than documented and than the connectivities were computed from.

Rebuild `.distances` from the truncated indices/distances for every
transformer when `knn=True`, as the shortcut path already did.

Closes #3809

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
